ne","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for the chosen approach and name the exact typed surface to reuse (e.g. the per-key coercers in _SECTIONS) and how it composes with the existing scan_tombstones aggregation without duplicating tombstone/alias handling.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.701,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan describes the desired outcome ('validate the full supported configuration surface, including typed coercion and enum constraints') but gives no rationale for the chosen mechanism nor names coerce_sparse vs a per-key loop","coerce_sparse (_config_schema.py:648-680) additionally handles _RESERVED_SECTIONS skips, alias resolution, and raise_or_warn_cfg_key tombstone routing — reusing it wholesale would overlap with scan_tombstones and abort on first error"],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for its chosen approach (why validate through the typed coercer surface vs. alternatives), nor which typed surface to reuse (the whole coerce_sparse path vs. a per-key coercer loop), leaving a load-bearing decision underspecified given coerce_sparse also applies alias/tombstone/unknown-key handling and raising semantics.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7c1f3d1863b75761","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Expected / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n4fd4c7588f44d16d","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reuses coerce_sparse to validate, unintentionally double-reporting or dropping tombstones that scan_tombstones already reports"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"y